    "Have you been to Latin America?": ["Have you been to Latin America? You should try the street food.","¿Has estado alguna vez en Latinoamérica? Tienes que probar la comida callejera."],
    "By the way": ["By the way, did you see the game last night?","Por cierto, ¿viste el partido anoche?"],
    "I'm bored.": ["I'm bored. Do you want to go for a walk?","Estoy aburrido. ¿Vamos a dar un paseo?"],
    "I'm nervous.": ["I'm nervous about my job interview tomorrow.","Estoy nerviosa por la entrevista de trabajo de mañana."],
    "I can't wait!": ["We're going to Hawaii next week. I can't wait!","La semana que viene nos vamos a Hawái. ¡Qué ganas!"],
    "That color looks good on you.": ["That color looks good on you. You should wear it more often.","Ese color te queda bien. Deberías ponértelo más seguido."],
    "You made my day!": ["Thanks for the cookies. You made my day!","Gracias por las galletas. ¡Me alegraste el día!"],
    "Let me know if you have any questions.": ["I've attached the slides. Let me know if you have any questions.","Te adjunto las diapositivas. Avísame si tienes alguna pregunta."],
    "Could you send me the file by Friday?": ["Could you send me the file by Friday? I need it for the presentation.","¿Me puedes enviar el archivo a más tardar el viernes? Lo necesito para la presentación."],
    "Let's touch base next week.": ["Let's touch base next week and see how things are going.","Hablemos un momento la próxima semana para ver cómo va todo."],
    "I'm working from home today.": ["I'm working from home today, so let's meet on Zoom.","Hoy trabajo desde casa, así que nos vemos por Zoom."],
    "Can I call you back?": ["I'm driving right now. Can I call you back?","Estoy manejando. ¿Te llamo después?"],
    "Is breakfast included?": ["Is breakfast included, or is it extra?","¿El desayuno está incluido o se paga aparte?"],
